WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.912
A hormone is a chemical carried in the blood to a target organ. The pituitary gland in the brain makes FSH and LH. They act on the ovary. The ovary then makes oestrogen and progesterone, which act on the uterus.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:28.943
In males, the testes make testosterone. It makes the male sex organs and the male sex characteristics develop, like a deeper voice. Oestrogen does the same job for female characteristics.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:47.031
This graph shows the menstrual cycle, about twenty-eight days. Early in the cycle, FSH rises. FSH makes a follicle mature. A follicle is a small sac in the ovary with an egg inside. FSH also makes the ovary release oestrogen.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.808
Oestrogen rises next. It repairs and thickens the lining of the uterus, after the last period.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:06.005
In the middle of the cycle, there is a surge of LH: it rises very fast. This triggers ovulation. Ovulation is the release of an egg from the ovary, around day fourteen.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:21.128
After ovulation, the empty follicle becomes the corpus luteum. It makes progesterone. Progesterone keeps the lining thick. When progesterone falls, the lining breaks down. This is menstruation, a period.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:35.972
Here is the method as a table. Say where each hormone is made. Then give one strong verb. FSH matures. LH triggers. Oestrogen repairs. Progesterone maintains. Testosterone develops.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:46.473
Now a real exam question. Oxytocin and LH are two hormones found in females. Describe the functions of LH. Two marks.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:55.626
LH has two jobs. Job one: the surge of LH in the middle of the cycle triggers ovulation. The ovary releases an egg.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:03.944
Job two: after ovulation, LH keeps the corpus luteum working. So the corpus luteum makes progesterone.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:11.311
Here is the full answer. Explanation by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:20.493
A common mistake is to say FSH causes ovulation. FSH matures the follicle. LH triggers ovulation.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:27.941
Another mistake is to say oestrogen keeps the lining during pregnancy. That is mainly progesterone.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:38.671
Your turn. A woman's pituitary gland makes too little FSH. Suggest why she may find it hard to become pregnant. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:47.160
FSH makes a follicle mature. With too little FSH, the follicles stay small, so no egg becomes mature.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:03:01.595
With no mature egg, there is no ovulation. So there is no egg for a sperm to fertilise, or join with. Also, FSH makes the ovary release oestrogen. With less oestrogen, the lining is not built up.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:12.689
So every time: which gland makes it and where does it act? Give one strong verb. For two marks, give a second job. And if a hormone is missing, its job does not happen.
